.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_PKEY_CTX_GET0_LIBCTX 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_PKEY_CTX_get0_libctx ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY_CTX_get0_propq ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY_CTX_get0_provider
.Nd functions for getting diverse information from an EVP_PKEY_CTX
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/evp.h
.Ft OSSL_LIB_CTX *
.Fo EVP_PKEY_CTX_get0_libctx
.Fa "EVP_PKEY_CTX *ctx"
.Fc
.Ft const char *
.Fo EVP_PKEY_CTX_get0_propq
.Fa "const EVP_PKEY_CTX *ctx"
.Fc
.Ft const OSSL_PROVIDER *
.Fo EVP_PKEY_CTX_get0_provider
.Fa "const EVP_PKEY_CTX *ctx"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_get0_libctx
and
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_get0_propq
obtain the OSSL_LIB_CTX and property query string values respectively
that were associated with the EVP_PKEY_CTX when it was constructed.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_get0_provider
returns the provider associated with the ongoing
.Vt EVP_PKEY_CTX
operation.
If the operation is performed by en
.Sy ENGINE ,
this function returns NULL.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_get0_libctx
and
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_get0_propq
functions return the OSSL_LIB_CTX and property query string associated
with the EVP_PKEY_CTX or NULL if they are not set.
The returned values should not be freed by the caller.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_get0_provider
returns a provider if an operation performed by a provider is ongoing,
otherwise NULL.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_PKEY_CTX_new 3
.Sh HISTORY
All functions were added in OpenSSL 3.0.
